<title>GREECE: TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</title>
<headline>TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ionian Bank reported the</p>
<p>following daily and year-to-date changes in the volume of Greek</p>
<p>mutual fund outstanding shares, net assets and net share prices,</p>
<p>as well as total net asset sizes as of May 13.</p>
<p>				    May 13/May 12   May 13/Dec 31, 96</p>
<p>						 (%)		  (%)</p>
<p>NET SHARE PRICES*</p>
<p>  Total market			    0.04		 6.09</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds  0.04		 4.50</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.20		 8.60</p>
<p>  Growth Funds			    0.03		51.06</p>
<p>* Prices include distributed dividends</p>
<p>VOLUME OF SHARES</p>
<p>  Total market			   -0.79		30.12</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds -0.84		31.02</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.09		 7.83</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    0.35		17.61</p>
<p>NET ASSETS</p>
<p>  Total market			   -0.74		36.23</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds -0.82		35.41</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.35		14.37</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    0.46		74.06</p>
<p>All calculations are based on a performance index of mutual</p>
<p>funds whose base was set to be equal to 100 on December 31,</p>
<p>1991.</p>
<p>NET ASSET SIZES (in drachmas)</p>
<p>  Total market				  5,180,845,932,568</p>
<p>  Fixed income funds			  1,884,989,608,554</p>
<p>  Money market funds			  2,992,410,780,955</p>
<p>  International funds			    89,911,552,876</p>
<p>  Growth funds				    213,533,990,184</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
